  "commands": [
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R01 — Create a fresh detached review-only clone and verify the exact successor, parent, tree, clean source and two-file delta.",
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R02 — Recompute the 268 review input hashes; confirm 266 are unchanged from the prior security pass and all 234 protected source files retain their pinned bytes. Reuse prior catalog, owner-provenance, evidence-pin and non-runtime observations only for unchanged content.",
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R03 — Rerun the original independent three-case probe without changing its source. The extra promotion now refuses and the baseline is read exactly once; the exact transition remains accepted.",
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R04 — Run two additional independent probes that replace the original baseline buffer with valid extra-promotion JSON during a later document lookup. The extra transition refuses and the original exact target still succeeds from the verified private snapshot.",
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R05 — Reproduce all four focused specification-lock and protocol test files, including three real-filesystem CLI cases: 27 tests, 143 assertions, zero failures and 100 percent function/line coverage for the covered gate modules.",
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R06 — Inspect snapshot construction before hashing and parsing from the internal document map; verify that caller lookups or later buffer changes cannot replace the verified baseline and that no new permission or source-adoption path is introduced.",
    "SEC-LOCK-FIX-R07 — Validate the public verdict against the original review-verdict.v0.1 validator and exact assigned job; verify public metadata boundaries, preserved historical rejection and clean detached source after review."
  ],
  "findings": {
    "blocking": [],
    "major": [],
    "minor": [],
    "nonBlocking": [
      {
        "title": "SEC-LOCK-01 resolved — verified document snapshots are copied before hashing and used without rereading caller input",
        "detail": "tools/quality/specification-lock.ts now reads each protected document once, creates an independent byte copy, verifies that copy and retains it in a private map. The baseline is parsed from that verified snapshot. The unchanged original independent probe now refuses the sixteenth promotion with one baseline read. Two additional probes confirm that replacing the caller-owned baseline buffer with different valid JSON during a subsequent lookup neither permits an extra promotion nor changes the accepted exact transition. The prior reject remains immutable; this resolution is bound only to the successor commit."
      }
    ]
  },
  "residualRisks": [
    "This is a dedicated security approval for the bounded Specification Lock successor, not catalog integration, consumer implementation, runtime data-processing admission, an execution capability or authorization to start a real mission.",
    "The prior security rejection is preserved and its unaffected observations are reused explicitly after 266 unchanged review hashes and the exact two-file delta were verified. Historical candidate-role attestations retain their original commits and scopes; heavy suites associated with them were not rerun here.",
    "The fixed evidence digest authenticates exact reviewed bytes, not a human identity. The bounded continuation mandate and independent promotion control remain separate from the audit JSON; no signature, approval timestamp, production issuer or runtime permission is fabricated.",
    "The actual fifteen-transition catalog, 105 unchanged entries, 114 locked/six candidate counts, four pinned candidate-role records and exact owner protocol source are unchanged from the prior verified target. Consumer HTTP, authority adapters, RLS/CAS/races, reference finality, retention/deletion/restore, browser and executor qualification remain absent as recorded by the consumer matrix.",
    "This fix secures the reviewed in-process byte-snapshot boundary. It does not establish an operating-system sandbox or an atomic filesystem snapshot against concurrent directory writers. The CLI regular-file, size, symlink and content-free error behavior remains covered by the targeted tests.",
    "Full repository, remote PR and post-merge gates were not rerun by this focused pass. Their exact-successor evidence and the remaining promotion roles/integration decision must be evaluated separately; this verdict does not claim a completed protected merge."
  ],
  "verdict": "approve",
